 "applies_to": "YORK YSAA air-cooled screw chillers (two refrigerant systems) with the 031-02550 board and its native BAS port.",
 "summary": "YORK by Johnson Controls YSAA chillers have BACnet MS/TP, Modbus RTU and N2 built into the 031-02550 board, so no gateway is needed. The BAS writes the remote setpoint and start/stop (AV 1, BV 1). Everything else is read-only analog and binary inputs: chilled liquid and ambient temperatures, per-system suction and discharge pressures and temperatures, EEV output, slide valve status, timers, cutouts, operational and fault codes, and system alarms.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Y.ACS.50.01 (031-03635-001)",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Access follows the sheet's sections: analog and binary write points (AV, BV) and read-only points (AI, BI).",
  "The sheet marks each point Standard or Not available for the listed firmware. The 15 points marked Not available (suction-pressure-unit setpoints and start/stops AV 2-4, BV 2-3, AI 4, AI 27, AI 33, AI 35-37, AI 44-45, and hot gas bypass BI 19-20) are left out.",
  "Values that don't apply to the unit's configuration are sent as zero.",
  "Operational and fault codes are numeric AIs; the states list the code values from the sheet's code tables.",
  "Units shown are imperial; SI units are in the sheet (pressures in bar)."
 ],
